WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:05.051 --> 00:00:07.851
Hello, hello, hello, and welcome

00:00:07.851 --> 00:00:09.731
to English Learning for Curious

00:00:09.731 --> 00:00:12.421
Minds, by Leonardo English, the show

00:00:12.441 --> 00:00:14.191
where you can listen to fascinating

00:00:14.191 --> 00:00:16.731
stories and learn weird and wonderful

00:00:16.741 --> 00:00:18.721
things about the world at the same

00:00:18.721 --> 00:00:20.371
time as improving your English.

00:00:20.741 --> 00:00:23.671
I'm Alastair Budge, and today we

00:00:23.711 --> 00:00:26.001
are going to the Comoros Islands,

00:00:26.001 --> 00:00:28.881
a tiny, remote archipelago in the

00:00:28.921 --> 00:00:31.921
Indian Ocean which became the unlikely

00:00:31.921 --> 00:00:34.141
setting for one of the strangest

00:00:34.141 --> 00:00:36.101
stories of the twentieth century.

00:00:36.561 --> 00:00:39.391
It's the story of a French mercenary who

00:00:39.391 --> 00:00:42.321
staged four coups in the same country,

00:00:42.691 --> 00:00:45.391
converted to Islam, took a new name,

00:00:45.651 --> 00:00:47.821
built a farm, was shot in the head

00:00:47.931 --> 00:00:50.571
twice, controlled the entire country

00:00:50.761 --> 00:00:53.421
from behind the scenes for over a decade,

00:00:53.701 --> 00:00:55.741
but then it all went terribly wrong.

00:00:56.131 --> 00:00:58.231
OK then, let's not waste a

00:00:58.261 --> 00:01:00.651
minute and get right into it.

00:01:02.201 --> 00:01:05.271
I'm going to go out on a limb and say

00:01:05.501 --> 00:01:08.371
that I imagine you might not know all

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.801
that much about the Comoros Islands.

00:01:11.341 --> 00:01:13.381
If you could place them on a map,

00:01:13.861 --> 00:01:15.781
you're probably ahead of most people.

00:01:16.611 --> 00:01:19.011
They are the small group of islands

00:01:19.221 --> 00:01:21.911
in the Indian Ocean, about halfway

00:01:22.121 --> 00:01:24.651
between Madagascar and Mozambique,

00:01:24.941 --> 00:01:27.241
off the eastern coast of Africa.

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:30.801
They are pretty small, roughly

00:01:30.811 --> 00:01:33.341
the size of London, and have this

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:36.711
volcanic landscape: steep peaks,

00:01:36.921 --> 00:01:40.421
dense jungle, and black lava fields.

00:01:41.151 --> 00:01:42.621
Culturally, they have been

00:01:42.621 --> 00:01:45.501
shaped by centuries of African,

00:01:45.751 --> 00:01:47.871
Arab, and French influence.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:51.691
Traders and settlers landed and made

00:01:51.691 --> 00:01:56.104
their bases over the years, and in 1886,

00:01:56.294 --> 00:01:59.291
France took formal control of the islands.

00:01:59.661 --> 00:02:01.871
It would govern them as part of its

00:02:01.931 --> 00:02:04.971
overseas empire for nearly ninety years.

00:02:05.881 --> 00:02:10.481
But by the early 1970s, independence

00:02:10.781 --> 00:02:14.281
was clearly coming, and this corner of

00:02:14.281 --> 00:02:16.841
the Indian Ocean was about to become the

00:02:16.841 --> 00:02:19.911
setting for something far less peaceful.

00:02:21.451 --> 00:02:24.801
In 1973, the French government and

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:27.211
the Comorian leaders had reached

00:02:27.251 --> 00:02:29.141
an agreement: there would be a

00:02:29.141 --> 00:02:30.921
referendum the following year.

00:02:31.881 --> 00:02:34.891
And sure enough, the referendum was

00:02:34.891 --> 00:02:38.751
held in 1974, with an overwhelming

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:41.721
majority voting for independence.

00:02:42.341 --> 00:02:46.501
But one of the four islands, Mayotte,

00:02:46.931 --> 00:02:50.261
did not vote for independence, instead

00:02:50.661 --> 00:02:53.091
preferring to remain part of France.

00:02:54.221 --> 00:02:56.691
This kicked off new discussions,

00:02:56.921 --> 00:02:59.031
more complications that we don't need

00:02:59.041 --> 00:03:02.221
to go into for this story, but the

00:03:02.221 --> 00:03:05.861
thing to understand is this: France

00:03:06.001 --> 00:03:08.731
was still dragging its feet, and

00:03:08.991 --> 00:03:11.981
the head of the government under the

00:03:12.001 --> 00:03:14.901
territorial system, a man named Ahmed

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:18.261
Abdallah, decided he had had enough.

00:03:19.571 --> 00:03:24.231
On the 6th of July 1975, he stood

00:03:24.301 --> 00:03:26.801
before the Comorian parliament and

00:03:26.851 --> 00:03:29.921
declared independence, unilaterally,

00:03:30.251 --> 00:03:32.801
without waiting for France's blessing.

00:03:34.121 --> 00:03:36.781
France was not best pleased.

00:03:37.421 --> 00:03:39.171
It didn't immediately recognise

00:03:39.171 --> 00:03:41.651
the new country, and it withdrew

00:03:41.931 --> 00:03:44.001
most of its financial support.

00:03:45.051 --> 00:03:47.581
And Ahmed Abdallah, well,

00:03:48.031 --> 00:03:49.371
he didn't last a month.

00:03:50.151 --> 00:03:53.321
After 27 days, he had been booted out

00:03:53.341 --> 00:03:56.401
of office in a coup led by a French

00:03:56.411 --> 00:03:58.981
mercenary called Robert Denard.

00:04:00.161 --> 00:04:02.981
Now, we will come to the coup, and the

00:04:03.011 --> 00:04:06.261
other coups, in a minute, but first let

00:04:06.261 --> 00:04:08.921
me paint you a picture of Robert Denard.

00:04:10.071 --> 00:04:14.341
He was born in 1929, in a small village

00:04:14.551 --> 00:04:17.251
in the Gironde, in southwest France.

00:04:18.421 --> 00:04:20.271
He was not from a military

00:04:20.271 --> 00:04:23.091
family, and he had no formal

00:04:23.091 --> 00:04:25.271
military education to speak of.

00:04:25.758 --> 00:04:29.001
But what he did have, from a young age,

00:04:29.211 --> 00:04:33.591
was a taste for action and a very flexible

00:04:33.591 --> 00:04:36.431
relationship with the idea of loyalty.

00:04:37.641 --> 00:04:40.011
He joined the French Navy as a

00:04:40.011 --> 00:04:42.831
young man, and then like hundreds of

00:04:42.831 --> 00:04:45.061
thousands of other young French men,

00:04:45.511 --> 00:04:48.411
served during the First Indochina War.

00:04:49.371 --> 00:04:52.511
So far, nothing particularly outrageous.

00:04:53.721 --> 00:04:55.921
He had clearly started to go down a

00:04:55.931 --> 00:04:59.121
slightly different path, however, as he

00:04:59.121 --> 00:05:02.231
was convicted of plotting to assassinate

00:05:02.431 --> 00:05:05.204
the French Prime Minister in 1954,

00:05:05.511 --> 00:05:08.761
and sentenced to 14 months in jail.

00:05:09.591 --> 00:05:12.621
On his release, he tried his hand at

00:05:12.621 --> 00:05:14.651
a more conventional life, becoming

00:05:14.651 --> 00:05:17.441
a salesman, but it wasn't for him.

00:05:18.291 --> 00:05:21.121
Life outside of Metropolitan France,

00:05:21.361 --> 00:05:24.161
it seemed, offered more excitement,

00:05:24.211 --> 00:05:26.711
more opportunities for adventure.

00:05:27.591 --> 00:05:29.921
He joined the colonial police in Morocco.

00:05:30.321 --> 00:05:33.961
And by the early 1960s, he had found his

00:05:33.961 --> 00:05:37.081
way into a very different kind of work.

00:05:38.361 --> 00:05:40.661
The Congo was falling apart.

00:05:41.281 --> 00:05:43.451
Belgium had granted the Congo

00:05:43.461 --> 00:05:46.671
independence in 1960, and within

00:05:46.681 --> 00:05:49.051
weeks the country was in crisis.

00:05:49.301 --> 00:05:52.061
Separatist movements, rival governments,

00:05:52.121 --> 00:05:54.461
a military that could barely hold itself

00:05:54.461 --> 00:05:57.271
together, and a prime minister who had

00:05:57.271 --> 00:05:59.831
been assassinated with the involvement of

00:05:59.841 --> 00:06:02.691
both Belgian and American intelligence.

00:06:04.031 --> 00:06:06.361
Into this chaos came a

00:06:06.361 --> 00:06:07.961
new kind of professional.

00:06:08.661 --> 00:06:09.441
The mercenary.

00:06:09.841 --> 00:06:11.800
And of course, Robert Denard.

00:06:13.261 --> 00:06:16.621
He arrived in 1961, after being

00:06:16.621 --> 00:06:18.781
recruited by a fellow Frenchman

00:06:18.961 --> 00:06:20.896
to fight for the secessionists.

00:06:21.241 --> 00:06:23.621
He was thirty-two years old, and it

00:06:23.631 --> 00:06:26.531
seemed that he had found his calling.

00:06:28.061 --> 00:06:30.691
Over the next fifteen years he

00:06:30.691 --> 00:06:33.441
fought in the Congo, in Biafra

00:06:33.441 --> 00:06:35.001
during the Nigerian Civil War,

00:06:35.291 --> 00:06:38.921
in Yemen, Benin, Chad and Angola.

00:06:39.431 --> 00:06:41.531
He organised coups, he trained

00:06:41.561 --> 00:06:43.841
militias, he led men into

00:06:43.851 --> 00:06:46.361
battle across half a continent.

00:06:47.371 --> 00:06:49.731
There is little record of the details of

00:06:49.731 --> 00:06:52.621
what he actually did, for obvious reasons,

00:06:52.911 --> 00:06:56.691
but given how long he did it for, how in

00:06:56.691 --> 00:06:59.651
demand he was, and that he survived for so

00:06:59.661 --> 00:07:02.021
long, he must have been pretty good at it.

00:07:03.231 --> 00:07:06.311
And almost everywhere he went, he had

00:07:06.311 --> 00:07:10.101
something he could count on: the quiet

00:07:10.111 --> 00:07:14.161
backing, the implicit approval, of France.

00:07:15.401 --> 00:07:17.451
This was part of the French

00:07:17.461 --> 00:07:19.901
government's system of Françafrique.

00:07:21.121 --> 00:07:24.621
The idea was simple:  France would

00:07:24.621 --> 00:07:27.491
maintain its influence over its former

00:07:27.701 --> 00:07:30.821
African colonies not through direct

00:07:30.821 --> 00:07:34.311
rule, since that era was over, but

00:07:34.671 --> 00:07:37.851
through money, intelligence, and when

00:07:37.861 --> 00:07:40.770
necessary, through men like Bob Denard.

00:07:41.851 --> 00:07:44.641
And the mastermind of this, or rather

00:07:44.941 --> 00:07:47.501
the man with a direct line to both the

00:07:47.511 --> 00:07:50.481
French President and a vast network of

00:07:50.541 --> 00:07:53.271
informants, fixers, businessmen, and

00:07:53.281 --> 00:07:56.151
mercenaries, was called Jacques Foccart.

00:07:57.131 --> 00:07:59.221
He was reportedly known as

00:07:59.471 --> 00:08:02.531
Monsieur Afrique, or Mr Africa.

00:08:03.591 --> 00:08:05.771
Whenever something needed to be done

00:08:05.801 --> 00:08:09.151
in Africa, Foccart knew who to call.

00:08:10.141 --> 00:08:14.041
Importantly, this was always at an arm's

00:08:14.041 --> 00:08:15.931
length from the official government.

00:08:16.201 --> 00:08:19.262
Always with plausible deniability.

00:08:20.431 --> 00:08:23.751
And Bob Denard was one of Foccart's

00:08:23.791 --> 00:08:25.711
most reliable instruments.

00:08:26.591 --> 00:08:29.371
Now, Denard was not especially

00:08:29.731 --> 00:08:32.041
ideological, as will become apparent.

00:08:32.581 --> 00:08:34.701
He fought for whoever was paying,

00:08:35.081 --> 00:08:37.701
as long as the politics broadly

00:08:37.941 --> 00:08:39.731
aligned with French interests.

00:08:40.461 --> 00:08:42.471
What he wanted was action,

00:08:42.911 --> 00:08:44.651
autonomy, and money.

00:08:45.431 --> 00:08:48.171
For most of his life, he had all three.

00:08:48.951 --> 00:08:50.991
And even when things went

00:08:50.991 --> 00:08:53.441
wrong, he rarely paid the price.

00:08:53.851 --> 00:08:56.711
He was seriously injured four times,

00:08:56.821 --> 00:08:59.261
and was shot in the head twice.

00:08:59.711 --> 00:09:01.281
But he survived.

00:09:02.591 --> 00:09:06.891
In January 1977, he led a coup attempt in

00:09:06.891 --> 00:09:09.401
Benin that collapsed after three hours.

00:09:09.871 --> 00:09:12.001
A French court later sentenced

00:09:12.001 --> 00:09:13.991
him in absentia to five years'

00:09:14.021 --> 00:09:16.201
imprisonment, and a Beninese

00:09:16.211 --> 00:09:18.191
court gave him the death penalty.

00:09:18.911 --> 00:09:20.541
But neither sentence

00:09:20.601 --> 00:09:21.771
troubled him particularly.

00:09:22.301 --> 00:09:24.491
And this was a theme in his

00:09:24.491 --> 00:09:26.751
life; by the time he got into

00:09:26.751 --> 00:09:28.761
trouble, if he was ever caught and

00:09:28.761 --> 00:09:30.761
sentenced, he would be long gone.

00:09:31.711 --> 00:09:35.041
By 1975, he was forty-six years

00:09:35.041 --> 00:09:37.781
old, with bullet scars dotted over

00:09:37.871 --> 00:09:40.171
his body and a mercenary's career

00:09:40.331 --> 00:09:42.891
already behind him that most soldiers

00:09:42.891 --> 00:09:45.081
couldn't match in two lifetimes.

00:09:45.941 --> 00:09:49.571
Then someone called him about the Comoros.

00:09:50.561 --> 00:09:54.598
So, it is the 3rd of August 1975.

00:09:55.121 --> 00:09:57.461
Ahmed Abdallah has been president of

00:09:57.461 --> 00:09:59.791
the Comoros for twenty-seven days.

00:10:00.491 --> 00:10:03.621
Bob Denard arrives with a small group of

00:10:03.691 --> 00:10:06.641
mercenaries and removes him from power.

00:10:07.391 --> 00:10:10.751
The operation is almost comically swift.

00:10:11.224 --> 00:10:13.621
Abdallah is put on a plane to Paris.

00:10:13.771 --> 00:10:15.471
His government is dissolved.

00:10:15.811 --> 00:10:17.521
The whole thing is over

00:10:17.721 --> 00:10:19.611
before most Comorians have

00:10:19.641 --> 00:10:21.271
understood what has happened.

00:10:22.521 --> 00:10:25.321
Denard has been hired by a coalition

00:10:25.341 --> 00:10:27.761
of opposition political parties called

00:10:27.781 --> 00:10:30.451
the United National Front, six groups

00:10:30.681 --> 00:10:33.531
united mainly in wanting Abdallah gone.

00:10:34.441 --> 00:10:37.421
Their man, a figure named Said Mohamed

00:10:37.421 --> 00:10:40.211
Jaffar, is installed as president.

00:10:40.651 --> 00:10:42.541
He lasts five months.

00:10:43.471 --> 00:10:45.751
The problem is that the United National

00:10:45.751 --> 00:10:48.641
Front was always a loose arrangement.

00:10:49.101 --> 00:10:50.991
Among its members is a more

00:10:51.151 --> 00:10:53.731
radical faction, led by a

00:10:53.731 --> 00:10:56.014
socialist named Ali Soilih.

00:10:56.885 --> 00:10:59.151
Soilih has ideas.

00:10:59.331 --> 00:11:02.721
Very radical ideas, and no interest

00:11:02.771 --> 00:11:04.391
in sharing power with Jaffar,

00:11:04.649 --> 00:11:07.201
whom he considers too moderate,

00:11:07.271 --> 00:11:09.551
too willing to appease France.

00:11:10.561 --> 00:11:14.641
In January 1976, Soilih pushes Jaffar

00:11:14.651 --> 00:11:16.831
aside in another internal coup.

00:11:17.471 --> 00:11:19.871
And France cuts what little

00:11:19.871 --> 00:11:21.821
financial support it has left.

00:11:23.101 --> 00:11:26.191
And Ali Soilih, well he is

00:11:26.191 --> 00:11:27.701
an unconventional leader

00:11:27.951 --> 00:11:29.851
in almost every sense.

00:11:30.501 --> 00:11:32.951
In one of his first acts, he

00:11:32.951 --> 00:11:35.121
orders the burning of the French

00:11:35.151 --> 00:11:37.731
colonial archives, a dramatic,

00:11:37.991 --> 00:11:40.641
symbolic rejection of the old order.

00:11:41.431 --> 00:11:43.351
He nationalises land.

00:11:43.591 --> 00:11:45.201
He promotes the removal

00:11:45.231 --> 00:11:47.121
of the veil among women.

00:11:47.691 --> 00:11:50.321
He legalises cannabis, a drug he

00:11:50.321 --> 00:11:52.311
is personally a heavy user of.

00:11:53.121 --> 00:11:56.121
And he creates a youth militia.

00:11:56.801 --> 00:11:58.381
He calls them the Moissy.

00:11:58.831 --> 00:12:01.201
They are teenagers, trained

00:12:01.371 --> 00:12:03.401
by Tanzanian military advisers

00:12:03.531 --> 00:12:06.681
and armed with AK-47 rifles.

00:12:07.181 --> 00:12:09.441
He lowers the voting age to fourteen.

00:12:10.121 --> 00:12:12.231
He is a big fan of Chairman Mao,

00:12:12.521 --> 00:12:15.511
and this is his version of Mao's

00:12:15.521 --> 00:12:18.341
Red Guards, a cultural revolution in

00:12:18.341 --> 00:12:21.361
miniature, on three small volcanic

00:12:21.391 --> 00:12:23.151
islands in the Indian Ocean.

00:12:24.501 --> 00:12:27.031
The Moissy, as you might imagine,

00:12:27.421 --> 00:12:29.381
do not cover themselves in glory.

00:12:30.611 --> 00:12:32.561
Meanwhile, Soilih is

00:12:32.581 --> 00:12:34.541
losing his grip on reality.

00:12:35.151 --> 00:12:36.541
He is drinking heavily.

00:12:36.661 --> 00:12:38.161
He is using drugs.

00:12:38.451 --> 00:12:41.155
And he has begun consulting a witchdoctor

00:12:41.411 --> 00:12:43.951
for advice on matters of state.

00:12:45.241 --> 00:12:47.611
And this witchdoctor has some

00:12:47.681 --> 00:12:51.441
bad news for him: he tells Soilih

00:12:51.441 --> 00:12:53.421
that he will be overthrown by

00:12:53.431 --> 00:12:56.251
a white man with a black dog.

00:12:57.111 --> 00:12:59.651
Now, were I the sort of person

00:12:59.651 --> 00:13:01.341
who believed in prophecies from

00:13:01.341 --> 00:13:04.211
witchdoctors, I think I'd probably focus

00:13:04.361 --> 00:13:06.718
on the man rather than the dog part.

00:13:07.407 --> 00:13:10.071
Soilih, however, seemed more

00:13:10.071 --> 00:13:12.541
concerned about the canine aspect.

00:13:13.331 --> 00:13:15.861
He orders a campaign to kill every

00:13:15.861 --> 00:13:18.141
single dog on the Comoros Islands.

00:13:18.951 --> 00:13:20.561
The islands are scoured.

00:13:20.901 --> 00:13:22.681
Dogs are found and

00:13:22.811 --> 00:13:24.451
killed in large numbers.

00:13:25.241 --> 00:13:27.201
It does not, as you might imagine,

00:13:27.521 --> 00:13:29.471
resolve the underlying problem.

00:13:30.811 --> 00:13:34.931
And by 1978, the islands are in a pretty

00:13:34.991 --> 00:13:38.501
poor place: economically broken, starved

00:13:38.521 --> 00:13:41.211
of French support, and struggling to

00:13:41.211 --> 00:13:44.001
maintain any semblance of public order.

00:13:45.061 --> 00:13:47.541
Ahmed Abdallah, who has been living in

00:13:47.541 --> 00:13:50.941
Paris and plotting his return, he decides

00:13:51.151 --> 00:13:54.231
now is the time to take his country back.

00:13:54.991 --> 00:13:58.551
And the man he wants to help him is Bob

00:13:58.561 --> 00:14:01.541
Denard, the very same Bob Denard who

00:14:01.541 --> 00:14:05.271
removed him from power back in 1975.

00:14:06.181 --> 00:14:08.315
Fortunately for Abdallah, Bob

00:14:08.315 --> 00:14:11.221
Denard is more interested in getting

00:14:11.251 --> 00:14:14.071
paid than in holding a grudge, and

00:14:14.321 --> 00:14:16.861
he is more than happy to oblige.

00:14:17.991 --> 00:14:22.041
In May 1978, in the dead of night, a boat

00:14:22.071 --> 00:14:24.851
arrives off the coast of Grande Comore,

00:14:25.061 --> 00:14:27.641
the largest of the Comoros Islands.

00:14:28.394 --> 00:14:31.871
Denard steps ashore with fifty men,

00:14:32.241 --> 00:14:35.141
most of them former French paratroopers.

00:14:36.021 --> 00:14:39.261
He even, according to one report, brings

00:14:39.301 --> 00:14:42.441
a black dog with him, ensuring that the

00:14:42.441 --> 00:14:45.011
witchdoctor's prophecy will come true.

00:14:46.241 --> 00:14:49.021
The operation takes a matter of hours.

00:14:49.671 --> 00:14:52.201
Soilih's forces collapse almost

00:14:52.201 --> 00:14:54.032
without a fight, and Soilih

00:14:54.201 --> 00:14:56.381
is placed under house arrest.

00:14:57.491 --> 00:15:00.191
Sixteen days later, however, he is

00:15:00.351 --> 00:15:03.431
shot dead, reportedly while trying to

00:15:03.431 --> 00:15:06.051
escape, although few people believe it.

00:15:06.801 --> 00:15:10.001
Ahmed Abdallah is reinstated as president.

00:15:10.891 --> 00:15:13.941
And as for Bob Denard, well,

00:15:14.151 --> 00:15:16.301
something surprising happens.

00:15:17.221 --> 00:15:19.091
You might have thought this was just

00:15:19.091 --> 00:15:20.441
another contract for Bob Denard,

00:15:20.921 --> 00:15:22.841
and that he would be on the first

00:15:22.881 --> 00:15:25.111
plane out, waiting for his phone to

00:15:25.111 --> 00:15:27.421
ring and off on the next mission.

00:15:28.471 --> 00:15:28.791
No.

00:15:29.791 --> 00:15:31.621
Denard does not go home.

00:15:32.111 --> 00:15:32.911
He stays.

00:15:33.681 --> 00:15:35.901
He becomes a Comorian citizen.

00:15:36.241 --> 00:15:37.911
He converts to Islam.

00:15:38.441 --> 00:15:40.141
He takes a new name:

00:15:40.701 --> 00:15:43.105
Said Moustapha M'Hadjou.

00:15:44.031 --> 00:15:45.561
He marries a Comorian woman.

00:15:45.961 --> 00:15:46.737
Then another.

00:15:46.837 --> 00:15:47.421
And another.

00:15:47.991 --> 00:15:49.981
By the end, he will have seven

00:15:49.981 --> 00:15:51.931
wives and eight children.

00:15:52.901 --> 00:15:54.141
He builds a farm.

00:15:54.541 --> 00:15:57.941
1,800 acres of volcanic land,

00:15:58.191 --> 00:16:00.441
growing crops, raising livestock.

00:16:01.011 --> 00:16:03.851
He becomes, by all accounts, a genuine

00:16:03.851 --> 00:16:06.561
farmer, someone who gets up early and

00:16:06.701 --> 00:16:09.081
knows his land and takes pride in it.

00:16:09.981 --> 00:16:11.271
There is more to this, though.

00:16:11.801 --> 00:16:14.831
He has also been given command of the

00:16:14.831 --> 00:16:19.091
Presidential Guard, an elite 500-man unit.

00:16:20.061 --> 00:16:22.711
In practical terms, this means he has

00:16:22.711 --> 00:16:24.991
military control over the country.

00:16:26.191 --> 00:16:28.151
Now, Abdallah is still

00:16:28.151 --> 00:16:29.523
nominally president.

00:16:29.691 --> 00:16:31.841
He gives speeches, receives foreign

00:16:31.841 --> 00:16:34.271
dignitaries, travels abroad to represent

00:16:34.271 --> 00:16:36.401
the Comoros at international meetings.

00:16:36.881 --> 00:16:39.731
But the man who actually holds

00:16:39.731 --> 00:16:42.141
the power is the one commanding

00:16:42.141 --> 00:16:43.231
the Presidential Guard.

00:16:44.211 --> 00:16:45.641
And not only this.

00:16:45.991 --> 00:16:47.621
Denard has business

00:16:47.641 --> 00:16:49.461
interests across the islands.

00:16:49.821 --> 00:16:51.911
He owns a private security firm,

00:16:52.051 --> 00:16:54.391
which holds contracts to protect

00:16:54.411 --> 00:16:56.421
South African-funded hotels that

00:16:56.421 --> 00:16:58.111
are being built on the islands.

00:16:58.481 --> 00:17:00.731
He operates a profitable commercial

00:17:00.811 --> 00:17:02.861
air shuttle between the Comoros

00:17:03.061 --> 00:17:05.291
and apartheid South Africa, which

00:17:05.391 --> 00:17:07.061
was heavily sanctioned at the time.

00:17:08.511 --> 00:17:12.351
When journalists visit and ask him about

00:17:12.351 --> 00:17:15.851
his role, he is charming and unhelpful.

00:17:16.401 --> 00:17:17.751
He talks about his farm.

00:17:17.751 --> 00:17:18.971
He talks about his family.

00:17:19.451 --> 00:17:21.441
He is a Comorian now, he says.

00:17:21.891 --> 00:17:23.871
He deflects questions about the coup,

00:17:24.171 --> 00:17:26.921
about his mercenary past and about

00:17:26.921 --> 00:17:29.081
the true nature of his authority.

00:17:30.041 --> 00:17:32.401
One reporter describes him as looking

00:17:32.421 --> 00:17:34.855
less like a mercenary warlord than

00:17:34.855 --> 00:17:37.381
a prosperous farmer who just so

00:17:37.381 --> 00:17:40.041
happens to own a great deal of land.

00:17:41.211 --> 00:17:44.761
But by 1989, the arrangement

00:17:45.021 --> 00:17:46.741
is beginning to crack.

00:17:47.731 --> 00:17:49.091
Abdallah has been

00:17:49.091 --> 00:17:50.701
president for eleven years.

00:17:51.271 --> 00:17:53.991
He is older, and he has started to

00:17:53.991 --> 00:17:56.901
believe, perhaps with some justification,

00:17:57.341 --> 00:18:00.181
that he has built enough of a constituency

00:18:00.441 --> 00:18:03.291
to govern without Denard at his side.

00:18:04.251 --> 00:18:07.101
He signs a decree ordering the

00:18:07.101 --> 00:18:10.131
Presidential Guard to be disarmed and

00:18:10.301 --> 00:18:13.551
integrated into the regular armed forces.

00:18:14.341 --> 00:18:16.241
It is a direct challenge.

00:18:17.131 --> 00:18:21.181
If the decree goes through, Denard loses

00:18:21.241 --> 00:18:23.321
his military dominance over the islands.

00:18:23.721 --> 00:18:25.651
His five hundred men become

00:18:25.651 --> 00:18:27.931
soldiers in someone else's army.

00:18:28.771 --> 00:18:32.211
He becomes just a man on a farm with a

00:18:32.211 --> 00:18:34.881
Comorian name and a complicated past.

00:18:36.291 --> 00:18:39.540
On the 26th of November 1989,

00:18:39.831 --> 00:18:42.111
Ahmed Abdallah is sitting in his

00:18:42.141 --> 00:18:44.641
office at the presidential palace.

00:18:45.261 --> 00:18:46.791
A shot is fired.

00:18:47.451 --> 00:18:49.731
Abdallah is dead, while

00:18:49.731 --> 00:18:52.301
Denard is wounded in the hand.

00:18:53.021 --> 00:18:55.601
The official account is that a military

00:18:55.641 --> 00:18:58.641
officer, acting alone and without orders,

00:18:59.071 --> 00:19:01.461
entered the office and opened fire.

00:19:02.041 --> 00:19:04.248
Denard, loyal Bob Denard,

00:19:04.621 --> 00:19:07.011
managed to return fire but

00:19:07.271 --> 00:19:09.401
could not save the president.

00:19:10.221 --> 00:19:12.361
Now, there is plenty of evidence

00:19:12.581 --> 00:19:14.521
to suggest that this official

00:19:14.531 --> 00:19:17.411
version is a fabrication, and

00:19:17.661 --> 00:19:20.551
suspicion has long fallen on Denard.

00:19:21.391 --> 00:19:23.411
When he was eventually tried in

00:19:23.411 --> 00:19:27.151
France in 1999 for the killing, he was

00:19:27.271 --> 00:19:29.711
acquitted, for lack of direct evidence.

00:19:31.101 --> 00:19:34.101
In any case, this time, France

00:19:34.291 --> 00:19:37.811
decides that Denard has gone too far.

00:19:38.571 --> 00:19:41.901
French paratroopers fly to the Comoros.

00:19:42.521 --> 00:19:45.251
They do not arrest Denard, but they make

00:19:45.251 --> 00:19:48.081
it very clear that now is the time to go.

00:19:48.861 --> 00:19:51.121
He boards a plane for South Africa.

00:19:51.641 --> 00:19:53.131
He is sixty years old.

00:19:53.401 --> 00:19:55.531
He has children in the Comoros.

00:19:55.531 --> 00:19:56.441
He has a farm.

00:19:56.971 --> 00:19:59.501
He has a name, Said Moustapha M'Hadjou,

00:19:59.761 --> 00:20:02.231
that he has been using for over a decade.

00:20:03.581 --> 00:20:06.311
And he is forced to leave it all behind.

00:20:07.271 --> 00:20:09.661
Now, if you had thought that

00:20:09.661 --> 00:20:11.831
was the end of the story for

00:20:11.871 --> 00:20:14.191
Bob Denard, no, there is more.

00:20:15.651 --> 00:20:19.381
In 1995, aged sixty-six years old,

00:20:19.671 --> 00:20:22.301
he sets sail for the Comoros, along

00:20:22.301 --> 00:20:24.531
with thirty-three fellow mercenaries,

00:20:24.691 --> 00:20:26.711
for what will be his fourth and

00:20:26.711 --> 00:20:29.251
final coup in the Comoros Islands.

00:20:30.111 --> 00:20:33.081
Denard and his thirty-three men take

00:20:33.101 --> 00:20:35.911
the country in a matter of hours.

00:20:37.381 --> 00:20:38.841
The sitting president, Said Mohamed

00:20:38.841 --> 00:20:42.341
Djohar, is removed from power.

00:20:43.371 --> 00:20:46.921
But Denard hasn't reckoned on one thing.

00:20:47.381 --> 00:20:49.201
The world has moved on.

00:20:49.591 --> 00:20:50.671
France has changed.

00:20:51.421 --> 00:20:55.311
In 1978, France needed him in the Comoros,

00:20:55.311 --> 00:20:57.971
or so its politicians may have felt.

00:20:58.341 --> 00:21:01.671
In 1989, France wanted him out but

00:21:01.961 --> 00:21:03.631
was willing to be polite about it.

00:21:04.681 --> 00:21:07.931
In 1995, things are very different.

00:21:08.391 --> 00:21:09.982
The Cold War is over.

00:21:10.411 --> 00:21:12.791
The old logic of Françafrique

00:21:13.091 --> 00:21:14.571
might not have disappeared

00:21:14.871 --> 00:21:17.821
completely, but it has shifted.

00:21:18.571 --> 00:21:21.121
A French mercenary staging a coup

00:21:21.331 --> 00:21:23.701
in a small island nation is no

00:21:23.701 --> 00:21:26.841
longer a quiet intelligence asset.

00:21:27.091 --> 00:21:29.251
It's an embarrassment, reported on

00:21:29.261 --> 00:21:31.871
by journalists, criticised in the

00:21:31.871 --> 00:21:35.221
European press, and impossible to deny.

00:21:36.411 --> 00:21:39.091
On the 4th of October, six

00:21:39.091 --> 00:21:41.511
days after the coup, French

00:21:41.521 --> 00:21:44.081
paratroopers land on Grande Comore.

00:21:44.821 --> 00:21:47.146
The operation is called Azalée.

00:21:47.991 --> 00:21:49.801
There is no fighting.

00:21:50.583 --> 00:21:52.781
Denard knows what this means.

00:21:53.071 --> 00:21:55.001
The army that has, for most of his

00:21:55.001 --> 00:21:57.121
career, backed him quietly from a

00:21:57.121 --> 00:22:00.381
distance is now facing him directly.

00:22:01.721 --> 00:22:03.611
He surrenders at three in the

00:22:03.611 --> 00:22:05.744
morning on the 5th of October,

00:22:05.961 --> 00:22:07.601
and he is flown to Paris.

00:22:08.261 --> 00:22:11.591
He is charged, tried and convicted of

00:22:11.641 --> 00:22:13.661
belonging to a criminal conspiracy.

00:22:14.601 --> 00:22:17.751
In June 2006, he is sentenced

00:22:18.081 --> 00:22:19.531
to five years in prison.

00:22:20.421 --> 00:22:22.231
The sentence is suspended

00:22:22.471 --> 00:22:23.921
and he will serve no time.

00:22:24.681 --> 00:22:26.931
He dies on the 13th of October

00:22:27.161 --> 00:22:30.001
2007, aged seventy-eight.

00:22:31.181 --> 00:22:34.271
And as for the Comoros Islands, it

00:22:34.271 --> 00:22:36.301
remains one of the poorest and least

00:22:36.351 --> 00:22:38.291
developed countries in the world.

00:22:39.391 --> 00:22:42.221
Now, Bob Denard is not responsible for

00:22:42.381 --> 00:22:44.581
all of the woes of the Comoros Islands.

00:22:44.851 --> 00:22:47.611
He was, after all, a product of

00:22:47.631 --> 00:22:50.131
a system, a system that tacitly

00:22:50.131 --> 00:22:52.311
supported what he was doing, as long

00:22:52.311 --> 00:22:54.321
as it was useful to its interests.

00:22:54.881 --> 00:22:56.391
But it's hard to make

00:22:56.391 --> 00:22:57.771
the claim that he helped.

00:22:58.541 --> 00:23:00.851
Four coups, multiple presidents

00:23:00.891 --> 00:23:03.291
ousted, two presidents dead

00:23:03.441 --> 00:23:05.051
in suspicious circumstances.

00:23:05.611 --> 00:23:07.741
It's hardly surprising people called

00:23:07.741 --> 00:23:10.121
him “the wolf of the Indian Ocean”

00:23:11.631 --> 00:23:14.211
. OK then, that is it for today's episode.

00:23:14.441 --> 00:23:15.671
I hope it's been an interesting one

00:23:15.721 --> 00:23:17.451
and that you've learnt something new.

00:23:17.881 --> 00:23:19.391
As always, I would love to know

00:23:19.391 --> 00:23:21.101
what you thought of this episode.

00:23:21.391 --> 00:23:22.321
Have you heard of the

00:23:22.321 --> 00:23:23.541
Comoros Islands before?

00:23:23.801 --> 00:23:24.931
Have you ever been there?

00:23:25.351 --> 00:23:27.191
Let me know in the comments below,

00:23:27.501 --> 00:23:28.911
if you're listening to this somewhere

00:23:28.911 --> 00:23:30.961
where you can comment, and for the

00:23:30.961 --> 00:23:32.711
members among you, you can head right

00:23:32.711 --> 00:23:34.671
into our community forum, which is at

00:23:34.671 --> 00:23:37.371
community.leonardoenglish.com and get

00:23:37.371 --> 00:23:39.501
chatting away to other curious minds.

00:23:40.641 --> 00:23:42.481
You've been listening to English Learning

00:23:42.481 --> 00:23:45.181
for Curious Minds by Leonardo English.

00:23:45.521 --> 00:23:48.331
I'm Alastair Budge, you stay safe, and

00:23:48.331 --> 00:23:50.501
I'll catch you in the next episode.

